  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Luspatercept may be associated with Beta Thalassemia through a pathway involving Deferiprone, a known treatment for Beta Thalassemia. The indication links Luspatercept to Beta-thalassemia Intermedia and Beta-thalassemia Hbb/lcrb, both of which are subtypes of Beta Thalassemia, and these subtypes are further linked to Deferiprone. This implies that Luspatercept may exert a therapeutic effect on Beta Thalassemia through a mechanism that is not yet fully understood, potentially involving the regulation of beta-globin synthesis or other cellular processes. The overlapping indications with Deferiprone suggest a possible shared therapeutic target or pathway, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a potential repurposing of Luspatercept for Beta Thalassemia, but further research is needed to clarify the underlying biological interactions.",
